# Write of a new file: diff header carries the "new file" tag
# (writeDetails.NewFile) and a pure-addition count, "+N −0"
# (diffCountsRow omits the zero side... actually it omits when EITHER
# side is zero, so a new file's count reads as plain "+N" with no "−0" —
# see the discrepancy EXPECT below).
# design: Terminal.dc.html:196 (diff block, tag:'new file')
@faux testdata/faux/qa/tools-write-new-file.yaml
@fixture testdata/behaviour/design
@args --permission-mode acceptEdits

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE add the rate limiter file
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Added the rate limiter file/ 20
SHOT write-diff
EXPECT /edit/
EXPECT /rateLimit\.ts/
EXPECT /new file/
EXPECT /\+3/
# The task brief calls for "+N −0" per file, but diffCountsRow
# (transcript.go) omits a zero side entirely for a pure addition — this
# EXPECT is the design's stated shape and is expected to fail against
# kiln's current rendering, recording that gap.
EXPECT /\+3\s+−0/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
